ePixelRatio)` is called again on top of the previous transform, causing exponential scaling. The transform must be reset first.\\n\\nChange:\\n```\\n    this.canvas.width = this.width * window.devicePixelRatio;\\n    this.canvas.height = this.height * window.devicePixelRatio;\\n    this.ctx.scale(window.devicePixelRatio, window.devicePixelRatio);\\n```\\nto:\\n```\\n    this.canvas.width = this.width * window.devicePixelRatio;\\n    this.canvas.height = this.height * win\n<truncated 12444 bytes>","Role":"\"App.js Bug Fixer\"","TypeName":"\"code_fixer\""}},{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Prompt":"\"You are fixing bugs in the NexusMobility styles.css and index.html files at:\\n- C:/Users/Kartik Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/styles.css\\n- C:/Users/Kartik Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html\\n\\nRead both files fully first. Then apply ALL of the following fixes using edit_file. After all edits, reply with a numbered list of every fix you applied.\\n\\n## CSS FIXES (styles.css):\\n\\n### CSS FIX 1 — Tab view animation never fires\\nThe `.tab-view` has `display: none` when inactive and `display: block` when `.active`. CSS transitions cannot animate from `display: none` to `display: block` — the opacity/transform transition never fires. The element just pops in.\\n\\nThis is a known limitation. Add `animation` to the active state to provide a visual transition instead.\\n\\nChange:\\n```\\n.tab-view.active {\\n  display: block;\\n  opacity: 1;\\n  transform: translateY(0);\\n}\\n```\\nto:\\n```\\n.tab-view.active {\\n  display: block;\\n  opacity: 1;\\n  transform: translateY(0);\\n  /* FIX: Use animation since CSS transitions can't bridge display:none → block */\\n  animation: tabFadeIn 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThen add a new keyframe at the end of the file (BEFORE the closing of the file, after the last `}`), append:\\n```\\n\\n/* FIX: Tab view entrance animation */\\n@keyframes tabFadeIn {\\n  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }\\n  to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### CSS FIX 2 — Missing .receipt-content padding in modal\\nThe `#receipt-content-area` div has class `receipt-content` but there's no CSS rule for `.receipt-content`. The receipt items display without proper spacing.\\n\\nAdd this rule AFTER the `.modal-dialog-body` rule block (after the `}` that closes `.modal-dialog-body` around line 1496):\\n```\\n\\n/* FIX: Missing receipt content container styling */\\n.receipt-content {\\n  padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n  gap: 0.65rem;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### CSS FIX 3\n<truncated 5551 bytes>","Role":"\"CSS and HTML Bug Fixer\"","TypeName":"\"code_fixer\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
